      "title": "Determining an Amount at an Overflow Point"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "a3c3d3f5-179e-5f48-a8ad-33c2fc702385",
      ":question/problem": "A nutrient tank for a hydroponic greenhouse can hold up to $610gal$ of solution. Initially, it contains $270gal$ of nutrient solution with $72lb$ of dissolved nutrient. A more concentrated solution with concentration $0.8lb/gal$ flows into the tank at a rate of $30gal/min$, while the completely mixed solution drains out at a rate of $20gal/min$. Rounded to one decimal place, find the amount of nutrient in the tank at the moment it begins to overflow.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "64cea7ed-ec93-5608-b515-8ebc799f9b92",
