      ":question/problem": "A nutrient tank for a hydroponic greenhouse can hold up to $552gal$ of solution. Initially, it contains $240gal$ of nutrient solution with $80lb$ of dissolved nutrient. A more concentrated solution with concentration $0.5lb/gal$ flows into the tank at a rate of $24gal/min$, while the completely mixed solution drains out at a rate of $16gal/min$. Rounded to one decimal place, find the amount of nutrient in the tank at the moment it begins to overflow.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question.",
